{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact clean pushed head 50cffa6af392fee45c7c0cb5f16618b62892ec09.\n\nThe stated gates pass independently: gofmt -d on all changed Go files, git diff --check, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go mod verify, and go test ./... -count=1. The three previous stale freshness claims and the batch-preflight wording are repaired; the only remaining \"live and fresh\" hits at this head are unrelated custody-reconciliation identifiers.\n\nThe new write-boundary condition is nevertheless incomplete. internal/app/admission.go recordStaleness returns immediately when caller body.staleness is non-empty, while stale and staleness are not reserved admission fields. An ordinary state caller resting on a stale basis can therefore supply any non-empty staleness string and prevent admission from writing body.stale=true and the required reviewguard.StalenessNote. This contradicts the requested contract that stale admission records staleness through that shared note builder, and allows caller-controlled, incomplete durable audit text at the authority boundary. Add coverage for this case and make the admission-owned stamp non-spoofable while preserving the legitimate guarded-review and merge receipt paths.\n\nArchitecture: this changes the Workroom interpreter/application admission boundary, CLI/MCP adapters, and behavior documentation. The candidate correctly documents the intended contract, but the application boundary does not yet enforce its complete body representation; the contract is therefore not fully preserved.\n\nSecurity: retired-basis refusal, explicit override, and both guarded reassignment claim checks remain sound. However, a caller can currently suppress or forge the recorded staleness shape for a stale-basis state. It grants no completion authority, but it undermines the signed audit record the change explicitly promises. This unresolved boundary defect blocks approval.\n\nSimplification: keep one admission-owned construction for stale and staleness. Reserve those fields for ordinary state writes or set them unconditionally from the computed bases and pass an explicit internal note only for guarded review/merge. The focused rule and a regression test are simpler than preserving a caller escape hatch.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:15d7b4408bd47a6e57a133a4b6ad90bd9484acf1","head":"50cffa6af392fee45c7c0cb5f16618b62892ec09","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fde2373a09e5927f41d80de92f758b32076ad7bb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7ba66209e706f4280164d80261981dc51e58836e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}